    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="12.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 12.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12.1" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ leohtgescot gelæste man to candelmæssan; dó oftor se ðe wille.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And leohtgescot gelæste man to candelmæssan; do oftor se ðe wille.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And light-dues shall be rendered at Candlemas; he who so desires may give them more frequently.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And the dues for the lighting of the church are to be paid by Candlemas, but may be rendered more often if one wishes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Lichtschoss werde zu Lichtmess [2. Febr.] entrichtet; thu es öfter wer will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let light-dues be paid at Candlemas [2 February]; let whoever wishes pay it more often.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="265"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_19">VI Atr 19</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 19</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><ref target="clause:ICn_12">I Cn 12</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 19.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
